      "claim": "The second, third and fourth acceptance criteria introduce a `path` property, two new flags (`write_refused`, `unserializable`) and a shared warning-emitting function that do not exist in the base tree, so no `find:` can be pinned for any of their `wrong_versions` — the mutant generator can only locate and revert text already present in the base. The spec itself discloses that `witness` will report `skip` for all three, meaning coverage for those claims rests entirely on a human reading the `wrong_versions` prose rather than on a mechanically-run mutant. Only the first claim (editing `EventLog.append`'s existing body) has lines the mutant tooling can locate and revert. This is a real gap in automated enforcement for three of the four claims, and is exactly the kind of thing a person must decide about before the cell starts, not discover afterward when a near-miss implementation of claims 2–4 passes the suite anyway.",
      "criterion": null,
